{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3Grading","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3Grading","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":53,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.gmn_with_derived_hypercharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.gmn_with_derived_hypercharge","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L376-L376","doc":"GMN closes with the framework-derived hypercharge `Y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.sign_forced_by_bowtie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.sign_forced_by_bowtie","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L374-L374","doc":"the sign is the `⋈_K`-forced up/down orientation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.writhe_magnitude_is_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.writhe_magnitude_is_generation","kind":"theorem","line":372,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L372-L372","doc":"|κ| recovers the generation winding: κ splits as (generation)×(sign). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie.mk","kind":"ctor","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L369-L369","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.CanonicalWeakIsospinFromBowtie","kind":"class","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L345-L377","doc":"**Primary conjecture (open — deliberately NO instance).**\n\nThe arithmetic above is proved unconditionally.  What is *conjectural* is\nthat the writhe-sign grading `T₃` is the **canonical** weak isospin — i.e.\nthat there is a framework-intrinsic net-signed-crossing map\n`κ : Quark → ℤ`, arising from the *actual* canonical meson/`⋈_K` braids\n(not entered as data), such that:\n\n* `writhe_magnitude_is_generation` — its magnitude is the generation\n  winding (so the split is genuinely into (generation)×(sign));\n* `sign_forced_by_bowtie` — its sign is *forced* by the strong-isospin\n  `⋈_K` orientation (`pp = σ_g` positive ⇒ up-type positive), not merely\n  consistent with it;\n* `gmn_with_derived_hypercharge` — GMN closes with a *framework-derived*\n  hypercharge `Y` (the #4561 twist invariant), not the SM input used in\n  `gellMannNishijima`.\n\nContent-bearing (each field is a `∀`-quantified constraint in the shape of\nthe claim), and **no instance is provided**: constructing the canonical\n`κ` from the braid category and the derived `Y` is the open step, which\nreduces to the SU(3)-flavour / CKM sector.  A trivial `κ := signedWrithe`,\n`Y := hyperchargeLeft` would *fabricate* closure over this finite toy and\nis forbidden (§3b-tax: do not fabricate an instance to close an open\nprimary; the openness is physical, not formal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.partner_flips_T3_same_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.partner_flips_T3_same_generation","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L333-L341","doc":"**The partner map raises/lowers `T₃` by one unit at fixed generation** —\nthe `ΔT₃ = ±1` selection rule of the charged current, and a second\nwitness that `T₃` is transverse to `genWinding`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.partner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.partner","kind":"def","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L326-L331","doc":"The `SU(2)_L` doublet partner (up-type ↔ down-type within a generation)\n— the `W±` charged-current transition `u ↔ d`, `c ↔ s`, `t ↔ b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding_finer_than_gmn_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding_finer_than_gmn_data","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L310-L322","doc":"**The generation is strictly finer than the GMN data.**  `u`, `c`, `t` carry\nthree different windings but land on the *same* GMN row — the precise sense in\nwhich the relation is blind to the generation index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmn_check_has_two_distinct_rows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmn_check_has_two_distinct_rows","kind":"theorem","line":292,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L292-L308","doc":"**The GMN check has exactly two distinct rows.**  Every one of the six\nquarks maps onto one of `gmnRowUp` / `gmnRowDown`, and those two are distinct.\nSo `gellMannNishijima` is two independent equations restated six times — not\nsix confirmations.\n\nStated by exhibiting the rows rather than as a `Finset.card`, because `Rat`\ndecidable equality does not reduce in the kernel inside `Finset.image`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmnRowDown","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmnRowDown","kind":"def","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L289-L290","doc":"The down-type GMN row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmnRowUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmnRowUp","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L286-L287","doc":"The up-type GMN row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmn_data_factors_through_weakType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gmn_data_factors_through_weakType","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L272-L284","doc":"**Every GMN ingredient factors through the up/down-type bit.**  Two quarks\nof the same `weakType` are indistinguishable to `Q`, `T₃` and `Y` alike, however\ndifferent their generation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.hyperchargeLeft_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.hyperchargeLeft_constant","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L267-L270","doc":"The left-doublet hypercharge is constant across all six quarks — it carries\nno per-quark information into the GMN check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_eq_charge_minus_halfY","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_eq_charge_minus_halfY","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L241-L246","doc":"**GMN inverted: the derived `T₃` equals the SM value `Q − Y/2`.** Makes\nthe check explicit — the topological grading recovers exactly the weak\nisospin the SM assigns, for all six quarks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gellMannNishijima","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.gellMannNishijima","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L229-L239","doc":"**Gell-Mann–Nishijima holds for the topologically-derived `T₃`.**\n`Q = T₃ + Y/2` for every quark, with `T₃ = sign(writhe)/2` (derived from\nthe braid) and the SM `Q`, `Y`.  This is the check, not a definition:\nhad the sign convention or the `½` normalisation been wrong, it would\nfail.  It does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.hyperchargeLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.hyperchargeLeft","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L222-L227","doc":"The weak hypercharge of the **left-handed** quark doublet, `Y = 1/3`\n(the same for both members of a doublet). Entered as SM data here; its\ntopological derivation is the sibling hypercharge-twist attack (#4561).\nIn the GMN normalisation `Q = T₃ + Y/2`, `Y = 2(Q − T₃)` gives `1/3`\nfor every left quark. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.emCharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.emCharge","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L216-L220","doc":"The measured electric charges of the six quarks (SM data, in units of\n`e`). Up-type `+2/3`, down-type `−1/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writhe_pos_iff_upType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writhe_pos_iff_upType","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L209-L212","doc":"The sign of the writhe is the up/down type (definitional bridge). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_mem","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L203-L207","doc":"Every quark's `T₃` is exactly `+½` or `−½`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_orthogonal_to_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3_orthogonal_to_generation","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L185-L199","doc":"**`T₃` is orthogonal to generation, in general.** Whenever two quarks\nshare the generation winding but sit in different weak sectors, their\n`T₃` differ. So `T₃` is a nontrivial grading transverse to `genWinding`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_up_strange_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_up_strange_down","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L180-L183","doc":"Charm is up-type, strange is down-type — at the same generation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_strange_differ_T3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_strange_differ_T3","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L174-L178","doc":"**…yet carry opposite `T₃`.** The signed-writhe refinement separates\nthem: charm `+½`, strange `−½`.  This is the datum the unsigned winding\nlacked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_strange_same_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.charm_strange_same_generation","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L169-L172","doc":"**Charm and strange share the generation winding** (both `n = 5`) — the\nexact collision `winding_content_not_injective` records. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding_values","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L163-L167","doc":"Generation winding reproduces the `T(2,n)` dictionary values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L159-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_strange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_strange","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L158-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_down","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L157-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_top","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_charm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_charm","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L155-L155","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheType_up","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L153-L154","doc":"Bundled `simp` set for the six writhe-sign values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_strange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_strange","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_down","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L149-L149","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_top","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L148-L148","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_charm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_charm","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L147-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.writheSign_up","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.T3","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L135-L137","doc":"**Weak isospin `T₃ = sign(writhe)/2 ∈ {+½,−½}`** — the fundamental\nSU(2)_weak weight read off the crossing sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.weakType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.weakType","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L131-L133","doc":"**Weak-isospin sector = sign of the writhe.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.genWinding","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L126-L129","doc":"**Generation winding = magnitude of the writhe.** Derived from\n`signedWrithe`, not an independent datum. Reproduces the corpus\n`T(2,n)` indices `{3,5,7}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.signedWrithe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.signedWrithe","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L114-L124","doc":"**The one derived datum.** The *signed* writhe `κ = ±n` of a quark's\ncanonical `T(2,n) = σ₁^{±n}` braid.  Magnitude `|κ| = n` is the\ngeneration winding (`u,d = 3`, `s,c = 5`, `b,t = 7`, matching\n`lepton-meson-torus-knot-dictionary`); the sign is the `⋈_K`-inherited\norientation, **up-type positive, down-type negative**.  Everything\nbelow is read off this single map — `genWinding`, `weakType`, and `T₃`\nare all functions of it, so the grading is not a second postulate but\nthe sign-half of the object whose magnitude is already the generation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instDecidableEqWeakType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instDecidableEqWeakType","kind":"instance","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType.downType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType.downType","kind":"ctor","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType.upType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType.upType","kind":"ctor","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.WeakType","kind":"inductive","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L109-L112","doc":"The `ℤ/2` weak-isospin sector: up-type vs down-type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instFintypeQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instFintypeQuark","kind":"instance","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instDecidableEqQuark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.instDecidableEqQuark","kind":"instance","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.bottom","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.strange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.strange","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.down","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.down","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.top","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.charm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.charm","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.up","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark.up","kind":"ctor","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L105-L105","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.WeakIsospinT3.Quark","kind":"inductive","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/WeakIsospinT3Grading.lean#L103-L107","doc":"The six SM quark flavours. ","signatureChunk":0}]}